{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["The reason for <b>and the rabble that was among them craved a craving</b> is that they lacked nothing in the wilderness, for they had the manna to satiate them, and they would prepare from it various dishes of a very fine taste, as He will relate. But they conjured in their hearts a great craving, like those who crave to eat charcoal and dirt and putrid foods." "<b>And they said: Who will give us flesh to eat</b> — for not all the people had meat to eat every day, even though they ate of it many times, and some among them had livestock and the great ones ate of it according to the custom of camps and places of high prices. But concerning fish they said, \"We remember the fish\" (Numbers 11:5), like one remembering forgotten things, for they had not eaten fish from the day they left Egypt until now."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:11.911147723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}